# Docker build context exclusions for lapis/Dockerfile.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
#   Before this file, `docker build` was uploading ~773MB of context on
#   every build — 692MB of that was `logs/`, 66MB was `pgdata/`, plus
#   assorted keycloak_data/, session-data/, .git/. All runtime state
#   from local dev, none of it needed inside the image. `COPY . /app`
#   was baking that stuff into the image AND invalidating the source
#   layer whenever a log file changed.
#
# EFFECT
#   Build context: ~773MB → ~10MB
#   Image size:    slims by ~700MB (logs no longer baked in)
#   Push time to Docker Hub: dramatically faster (smaller layers)
#   Layer cache:   source COPY stays stable across log/data churn
#
# WHAT TO EXCLUDE
#   1. Runtime state generated by docker-compose / local dev
#   2. VCS / editor / OS junk
#   3. Docs / tests / assets that don't need to be in the image
#   4. Secrets (.env)

# ─── Runtime state (the giant offenders) ──────────────────────────────
logs/
pgdata/
keycloak_data/
session-data/
# Docker Compose leaves a docker-volume / bind-mount dir here on some
# setups — never useful inside the image.
docker-volume/

# ─── VCS / build cache / editor junk ──────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ─── Local dev config that shouldn't ship in the image ────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.sample.env
!.env.example
.env.local
.envrc

# ─── Docker configs (used only by docker-compose, not the image) ──────
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
Dockerfile.*
!Dockerfile

# ─── Docs + test artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────
docs/
*.md
!api-docs/**   # api-docs/swagger.json IS used at runtime
archive/
# Non-essential examples / debugging scripts kept out of the image
app copy.lua

# ─── Node modules that leak into the context if opsapi-dashboard/ is
# ───   checked out as a sibling (guard against future layout churn) ──
**/node_modules/

# ─── Bulky opt/ files if they aren't image-used ───────────────────────
# (leave `opt/` in-context — the Dockerfile COPY's it explicitly. If
#  everything in opt/ is code that ships, don't ignore it here.)
